  "scope": "Fixed4860-slot actual binary-fuel conversion and complete finite adaptive-state iteration. The controller traverses the produced unary cursor, executes the actual full step and retains the changing six-field state/event list on the same heap. The endpoint equals literal BinaryFractionalCore.runFrom.state, including padded-zero fuel and repeated stopped guards. Original capacities give additive unreduced weight/load/total width growth; candidate objective/best-cost widths stay polynomial. One instruction bound depends only on graph order, original demand count, original field/label width, numerical fuel and fuel bit length. Same-run physical accounting includes the terminal attempt and original heap/address bounds. No unary counter, intermediate choice/state or output is supplied. Original represented graph/current state/fuel/context and dimensions remain inputs. Raw preparation, initial delta/state/fuel construction, outer degenerate dispatch and complete paper runtime remain separate. Polynomial in numerical fuel is not claimed polynomial in its bit length alone.",
  "pending": [
    "independent source review",
    "new-source safety and official replays",
    "production integration and exact CI"
  ]
